{
  "case_id": "2004-03-636",
  "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Tuesday, November 2, 2004 The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:59 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case presents the issue of whether the California Department of Corrections, unlike every other State in the Federal Bureau of Prisons, may continue its more than 28-year, unexamined practice of routine, blanket racial segregation of its prisoners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is California the only State, to your knowledge, to apply this procedure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know if there are in these other States the same incidents of racial riots or racial killings or racial attacks?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Is -- is there an argument to be made that the reason we make that emphasis and -- and an argument for you in this case that there is somehow a greater fragility to -- to the effective standards to prevent racial classification than there is to the possibility of enforcing speech rights and so on? Is there something to worry about here more than in the case of -- of enumerated rights that -- that gets the Turner analysis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: This is not a permanent segregation in these California prisons. It's just temporary, isn't it? How long does it last?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Is there any evidence in the record that the initial placing of two inmates in the same cell has ever had -- has ever produced a racial incident?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. GRUNDER: There's nothing in the record, Your Honor. The policy has been in effect for a considerable length of time, and -- and during that time, they have not interracially housed inmates in the same cell."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That's what I don't understand too. That -- that's really what most troubles me about this case. Why -- why do you do this to the transferees at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. GRUNDER: There's a -- there's a couple of reasons, Your Honors. First of all, as much as you may know about the transferring individual, you may not know the information about their prospective cellmate at the transfer institution because they may be somebody who's a newly received cellmate, somebody who is going through a reception center process themselves."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. GRUNDER: It is -- yes, it is a practice. I wouldn't characterize it a policy. It's a practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And do we have any evidence to that effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, the reality in prison is that people are pressured to join gangs and to -- you either hang with your own or you don't and -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we do have in the record, Your Honor, is that the policy and the practice does not apply after the 60 days. Inmates are allowed to request a cell together and can choose their own cellmates so long as the other cellmate agrees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But there -- is there any figures on the prison population as a whole, the incidents of interracial violence as opposed to intraracial violence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do not agree with counsel. I believe that the Ninth Circuit did properly apply the Turner standard in this case and that California would pass and does pass the Turner test in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The purpose is multi-fold. First, yes, it is to protect the inmate from -- from having harm done to him in the cell, which is a very difficult area to protect. It's a small area and not easily visible into the -- into the cell directly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, why -- why should you use the Turner standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you accept that this is invidious discrimination on the basis of race?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Grunder",
      "case_id": "2004-03-636",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b0500cf76b47e1f4be75334729284c8b001b259a2a232d6197f7a73d5dba2c04",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b0500cf76b47-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't think it's invidious, Your Honor. As a matter of fact -\u00ad"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
